WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:01.730
What made you stop

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:12.890
scrolling?

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:17.350
Now, let's make something worth stopping

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:24.260
for. An object on your desk could be the
start of a whole campaign.

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:27.860
Even this. I'm going to use these
sunglasses for today's lesson and build an

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:30.360
ad around them. Let's start with a photo.

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:34.800
If you're taking your own photo, show the
whole object in clear light.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:38.530
Keep the edges visible. The reference
needs to tell us what the product

00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:43.560
actually looks like. Now, let's bring this
photo into Supercomputer.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:48.200
In a new chat, I'll click the plus and
choose Attach File.

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:52.020
Then I'll click Upload Media and select
our photo.

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:55.230
Before we build the campaign, I want a
clean product image.

00:00:55.260 --> 00:01:00.200
I type, remove the table, and put the
glasses on a plain background.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:03.300
Keep the glasses exactly as they are.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:06.740
For the new image, we're keeping the
frame, bridge, temples, and amber

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:09.880
lenses exactly the same, with no redesign.

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:13.580
Alright, it's ready. Let's put it next to
the original and check the shape.

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:18.130
I compare the outline, the bridge, and the
side of the frame with our

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:22.230
original. This gives us a clear reference
to use in the next steps.

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:27.610
So, one product photo, a photo shoot, and
two ways to make people notice

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:32.920
it. We're giving these sunglasses their
own moment of fame.

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:37.580
You'll make images you can actually use,
then turn them into a video.

00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:41.890
I'll show you a creator talking about the
product, and a short commercial

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:44.840
where the product does all the talking.

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:48.940
You can make either one, or both, if you
get carried away.

00:01:48.940 --> 00:01:51.230
Next, let's find someone to wear these.

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:54.100
In one ad, she'll talk about the glasses.

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:56.840
In the fashion commercial, she'll wear
them.

00:01:56.840 --> 00:02:00.280
I want someone who feels right for these
big blue frames.

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:05.400
If your idea only needs the product, you
can skip the casting.

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:10.410
I'm picturing a girl with two black buns,
a white tee, and gray cargo

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:13.720
pants. Let the glasses do the loud part.

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:16.230
Supercomputer has something called skills.

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:21.460
A skill is just a set of rules and
guidelines for a specific job.

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:26.100
People create and share them for things
like photo shoots, videos, and

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:30.600
writing. So, you can reuse those
instructions instead of explaining the

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:35.530
whole process every time. Type a slash to
see the available skills.

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:39.190
For our casting, I'll choose character
sheet.

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:44.000
I describe the person I have in mind, and
it works out the detailed prompts.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:48.130
Let's start with 20 different faces and
see who feels right for these

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:51.400
glasses. I'm trying 20 variations for this
demo.

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:55.560
You can start with fewer. I checked the
proposals before approving.

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:59.620
Soul 2.0 is our own image model here at
Hixfield.

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:03.920
I like it because it's really creative,
and it's super affordable.

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:08.230
A batch of 10 images here costs just one
and a quarter credits.

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:13.780
So, I'm going for 20, more options, and a
better chance of finding someone I

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:15.660
really like. Look at this.

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:18.180
We've got a whole cast to choose from.

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:22.660
Let's pick the one that could be our main
talent.

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:25.880
I'm going with her. She caught my eye
straight away.

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:30.370
The fitted tee, silver sneakers, and those
two buns feel right for our

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:34.420
sunglasses. A character sheet gives you
different views of the same person.

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:37.230
Full body on the left, her face on the
right.

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:40.660
I've left the 16x9 layout.

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:45.360
Now, we have her face and outfit to refer
to when we put her somewhere else.

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:47.420
Let's find her somewhere to shoot.

00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:49.220
Now, I'll look for street locations.

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:51.600
I want some options I could use for a
creator video.

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:55.500
I'm asking for 10 locations so I can
choose from actual pictures.

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:59.020
Let's hit approve and wait for our
generations.

00:03:59.020 --> 00:04:03.030
Oh, here it is. Let's review the
locations.

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:06.110
I'm not feeling these yet.

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:10.690
I want more color and a background that
really stands out.

00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:15.460
If the first try doesn't quite work,
that's normal.

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:18.040
Remember the loop from our earlier
lessons.

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:21.480
Idea, prompt, result, tweak.

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:26.580
Look at what you got. Choose one thing to
change and try again.

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:30.300
Keep using the techniques we've already
covered, and don't be afraid to play

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:33.230
with different models and try another
approach.

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:36.080
Okay, our second batch is ready.

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:41.490
Let's take a look. I'm still not seeing a
location

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:46.180
I really love. Let's generate 10 more.

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:49.140
Alright, three rounds in, I think we can
